**Your disk is 100% FULL.** That's why Postgres can't write — no space to create files. The log file doesn't even exist because Postgres couldn't write it.

This is why everything is failing.

## Free up space — run this one command

```bash
brew services stop postgresql@15 && rm -rf ~/Library/Caches/* && rm -rf ~/Library/Application\ Support/Caches/* && brew cleanup --prune=all && pip cache purge 2>/dev/null ; npm cache clean --force 2>/dev/null ; df -h / | tail -2
```

This:
1. Stops Postgres (safe shutdown)
2. Clears user caches
3. Cleans Homebrew old downloads
4. Clears pip cache
5. Clears npm cache
6. Shows new disk space

Should free 5-20 GB depending on how much accumulated.

## Then check space

```bash
df -h /
```

Look at the "Avail" column. Need at least 5GB free for Odoo + Postgres to work properly.

## Then restart Postgres

```bash
brew services start postgresql@15 && sleep 3 && psql -U odoo -l
```

Should list databases. If yes → ✅ restart Odoo in PyCharm.

